From bab29ac20ae313c565a79b7b1406956323ef686e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <james@generalinference.xyz>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:58:49 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: gate construction logs behind SKIPPY_LOG_LEVEL

The stage-planning test binaries build real llama contexts, and llama.cpp
logs every input-tensor edge of every graph reserve at DEBUG level through
the default callback that prints unconditionally. A single graph-contract
case wrote 81 MB of transcript; a full staged test run pushed CTest's
LastTest.log past 15 GB per build directory.

Add an internal log gate that forwards only messages at or above a
threshold to the previously installed callback. Every skippy test binary
that links the runtime installs it at startup with the threshold read from
SKIPPY_LOG_LEVEL (debug|info|warn|error, default warn), so agents debugging
graph contracts can restore the full firehose per run:
SKIPPY_LOG_LEVEL=debug ctest -R skippy_graph_contract
